{"name":"Green Darner Tail","hex":"#75bbfd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"green","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of grass and leaves; a primary additive color midway between yellow and blue which is evoked by light between roughly 495–570 nm.","A member of a green party; an environmentalist."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a green hue.","Sickly, unwell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/green"},{"term":"darner","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One who darns.","A needle used for darning, a darning needle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/darner"},{"term":"tail","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The caudal appendage of an animal that is attached to their posterior and near the anus or cloaca.","An object or part of an object resembling a tail in shape, such as the thongs on a cat-o'-nine-tails; a strand of material hanging from something."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To hold by the end; said of a timber when it rests upon a wall or other support; with in or into","To swing with the stern in a certain direction; said of a vessel at anchor."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tail"}],"entries":[{"title":"Green darner","blocks":[{"text":"The green darner or common green darner, after its resemblance to a darning needle, is a species of dragonfly in the family Aeshnidae. One of the most common and abundant species throughout North America, it also ranges south to Panama. It is well known for its great migration distance from the northern United States south into Texas and Mexico. It also occurs in the Caribbean, Tahiti, and Asia from Japan to mainland China. It is the official insect for the state of Washington in the United States."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Common_Green_Darner_Anax_junius_JG.jpg/330px-Common_Green_Darner_Anax_junius_JG.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green_darner","wikidata":"Q175808"},{"title":"Aeshnidae","blocks":[{"text":"Aeshnidae, also called aeshnids, hawkers, or darners, is a family of dragonflies, found nearly worldwide, with more than 50 genera and over 450 species."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Lesser_Tasmanian_Darner_Austroaeschna_hardyi_female.jpg/330px-Lesser_Tasmanian_Darner_Austroaeschna_hardyi_female.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aeshnidae","wikidata":"Q516862"},{"title":"Tail","blocks":[{"text":"The tail is the elongated section at the rear end of a bilaterian animal's body; in general, the term refers to a distinct, flexible appendage extending backwards from the midline of the torso. In vertebrate animals that evolved to lose their tails, the coccyx is the homologous vestigial of the tail. While tails are primarily considered a feature of vertebrates, some invertebrates such as scorpions and springtails, as well as snails and slugs, have tail-like appendages that are also referred to as tails."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/White-tailed_deer%2C_tail_up.jpg/330px-White-tailed_deer%2C_tail_up.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tail","wikidata":"Q60960"},{"title":"Green","blocks":[{"text":"Green is the color between cyan and yellow on the visible spectrum. It has 295–350 different shades. It is evoked by light which has a dominant wavelength of roughly 495–570 nm. In subtractive color systems, used in painting and color printing, it is created by a combination of yellow and cyan; in the RGB color model, used on television and computer screens, it is one of the additive primary colors, along with red and blue, which are mixed in different combinations to create all other colors. By far the largest contributor to green in nature is chlorophyll, the chemical by which plants photosynthesize and convert sunlight into chemical energy. Many creatures have adapted to their green environments by taking on a green hue themselves as camouflage. Several minerals have a green color, including the emerald, which is colored green by its chromium content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg/330px-Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green","wikidata":"Q3133"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Anax_junius.JPG/500px-Anax_junius.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Anax_junius.JPG/500px-Anax_junius.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnax_junius.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Img_041538_mating_anax_junius.jpg/120px-Img_041538_mating_anax_junius.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Img_041538_mating_anax_junius.jpg/250px-Img_041538_mating_anax_junius.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Img_041538_mating_anax_junius.jpg/120px-Img_041538_mating_anax_junius.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AImg_041538_mating_anax_junius.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Anax_junius-Laying_eggs-2.jpg/120px-Anax_junius-Laying_eggs-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&ut